{
  "_about": "Revision 1 of the subway-topology dataset: the committed subway registry file as production served it at commit d856f333 (captured 2026-10-20; the file is deleted), its platform directions keyed by platform id in the registry order, and its neighbors. The lines, stations and platform identities stay in code as SUBWAY_LINES and SUBWAY_STATIONS. Not trimmed. Revision 2 (2026-10-25, ADR 0022 D4), pushed to skku_content_dev from this checkout, adds the platforms of 사당 (S1-2-226, S1-4-433), 금정 (KR-1-P149, KR-4-443) and 종로5가 (S1-1-154), carries the line 1, 2 and 4 platforms' upstream, watched and next platforms to the wider stretches of subway-timetables revision 2, and adds those stretches' stops as neighbors (Seoul API and train-map names as both wrote them on 2026-10-25 12:23-12:27 KST). Renamed 2026-10-25 (owner decision): 성균관대's platform id KR-1-0153 became its KRIC code KR-1-P153 wherever it appears; no other value changed. Revision 3 (2026-10-26, ADR 0022 D5), drafted from this checkout and pushed after its deploy, gives every line 1 and 4 neighbor a station id (a slug of its English name in the Seoul SearchSTNBySubwayLineInfo) and its coords (the Seoul subwayStationMaster row of the same station code), so a journey ride can list the stops it passes; both APIs called once on 2026-10-26; no other value changed. Names added 2026-10-27 from production revision 4: every neighbor with a station id carries its name in every language (Seoul SearchSTNBySubwayLineInfo), as the push now requires; no other value changed.",
